리뷰 거절: internal/manifest/manifest.go:254 parseGradle was rewritten from a whole-content regex to a line-by-line scan (`for _, raw := range strings.Split(content, "
")` with `gradleDeclaration` at manifest.go:217 anchored `^...$`), so a declaration wrapped over more than one line is now dropped. The old regex `(implementation|...)\s*[( ]\s*['"]` let `\s*` cross the newline and read it. Verified by running both parsers on the same input: for `dependencies {
 implementation(
 "androidx.compose.ui:ui:1.5.0"
 )
 testImplementation (
 'org.mockito:mockito-core:5.3.1'
 )
 implementation "androidx.room:room-runtime:2.6.1"
}` the parser on main returns all three packages, HEAD returns only androidx.room:room-runtime. This wrapped form is normal Kotlin-DSL / formatter-wrapped Groovy style, so a repository that declares a library only that way silently leaves the inventory — the exact failure the commit message says it is fixing ('absent reads exactly like a repository that does not use the library at all'). Behaviour therefore contradicts the commit message, which describes the change as purely additive. / internal/manifest/manifest_test.go:258 neither new test covers a declaration split across lines, so the regression above is not caught; the added cases only exercise single-line shapes.
